# graphify knowledge-graph artifacts (generated outputs committed so contributors
# and Claude sessions can read the graph summary without rebuilding — see
# graphify-out/.gitignore for what stays machine-local).
#
# graph.json itself is NO LONGER COMMITTED (it outgrew GitHub's PR diff
# limit — see graphify-out/.gitignore), so the union-merge driver that used to
# be declared here is gone with it: two devs can no longer conflict on a file
# that is not in the index. `graphify hook install` still registers that driver
# locally and that is harmless — an attribute-less file just uses a normal
# merge.

# The committed graphify outputs are generated; mark them so
# GitHub collapses their (large, churny) diffs by default and excludes them from
# repository language statistics.
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md linguist-generated=true
graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json linguist-generated=true
